@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title Buildx driver selection — which driver, and where a FROM resolves

node "Maintainer host — Fedora or macOS" as HOST <<host>> {
  component "defs/lib/docker-build.sh\nproveo_docker_build" as LIB <<app>>
  component "proveo_docker_ensure_buildx\n<push|load> <platforms>" as SEL <<app>>
  component "proveo_docker_builder_running\nStatus-line health probe" as HEALTH <<app>>
  component "docker driver\nshares the daemon image store\ncannot cross-build" as DDOCKER <<app>>
  component "docker-container driver\nproveo-multiarch — own image store\ncross-builds any platform" as DCONT <<app>>
}

database "Local daemon image store" as LOCAL <<db>>
cloud "Registry" as REG <<cloud>>
component "Stale-parent build\n(silent: no error, no warning)" as STALE <<error>>

LIB ARROW_MAIN SEL : platforms resolved BEFORE the builder
SEL ARROW_MAIN HEALTH : candidate alive?
SEL ARROW_MAIN DDOCKER : ""--load"" · platform == host arch
SEL ARROW_CLOUD DCONT : ""--push"" · multi-arch publish
SEL ARROW_OPTIONAL DCONT : ""--load"" · cross-arch — warns first
DDOCKER ARROW_MAIN LOCAL : ""FROM"" resolves the image just built
DCONT ARROW_CLOUD REG : ""FROM"" resolves the PUBLISHED image
DCONT ARROW_ERROR STALE : cross-arch ""--load"" — a locally edited parent is invisible

note right of SEL
  **The driver is not a detail — it decides where ""FROM"" resolves.**

  | mode | platform | driver | parent comes from |
  | ""--push"" | multi-arch | docker-container | registry |
  | ""--load"" | host arch | docker | local daemon |
  | ""--load"" | cross-arch | docker-container | registry (warned) |

  ""--push"" taking the registry parent is //correct//: the published
  child must sit on the published base. A native ""--load"" must take
  the docker driver so an edited base actually reaches its dependents.

  Overrides: ""PROVEO_PLATFORMS"", ""PROVEO_BUILDX_BUILDER"" (container),
  ""PROVEO_BUILDX_LOCAL_BUILDER"" (docker driver).
end note

note bottom of HEALTH
  **Two traps, both of which silently disable the docker driver.**

  //Exit status is not health.// ""docker buildx inspect"" exits 0 for a
  builder whose endpoint is dead — a stale desktop-linux or default
  context on a machine running another engine still 'inspects' fine.
  Only the ""Status:"" line is the health signal.

  //Never pipe it into ""grep -q"".// Every ""defs/*/build.sh"" runs under
  ""set -o pipefail""; ""grep -q"" exits at the first match, docker dies of
  SIGPIPE, and the pipeline reports 141 — **a match reads as a
  failure**. Every healthy builder is then rejected and the whole fleet
  falls back to the container driver. Capture the output first, then
  test it with ""awk"" off a here-string, outside any pipeline.
end note

note bottom of DDOCKER
  **A docker-driver builder is usable only from ITS OWN context.** buildx
  refuses ""--builder <name>"" for a docker-driver builder that is not the
  current context, answering "use ""docker --context=<name> buildx"" to
  switch". So the current context — ""docker context show"" — is the only
  candidate; there is nothing to enumerate.

  Enumerating ""docker buildx ls"" and taking the first running
  docker-driver row is what trap #1 above punishes: on any machine
  carrying a leftover ""default"" or ""desktop-linux"" context — every
  OrbStack/Colima/Rancher box, and any Linux box that once ran Docker
  Desktop — that row inspects as running and then fails at build time
  with the context error. The asterisk marking the current builder was
  the signal, and blanking it before the field split threw it away.

  Only the ""--load"" host-platform path reaches this decision. A ""--push""
  or cross-platform build returns earlier on the container driver, so
  multi-arch distributables never depend on which context is current.
end note

note bottom of STALE
  **The symptom to recognise.** The child builds cleanly against a
  stale published parent — no error, no warning. It shows up only as a
  size inversion: ""proveo/base-node"" at 687MB on top of a 903MB
  ""proveo/base"". Every image must be larger than its parent.

  **A locally verified image is not proof about the pushed one** —
  ""--load"" and ""--push"" deliberately resolve different parents.
end note
@enduml
